  "guide_topics": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "lines": [
        "AIRTS is an AI Real-Time Strategy game built for the BlueOrange AI Jam.",
        "",
        "Two teams compete to destroy each other's Command Center. Each team can be controlled by a human player or an AI controller.",
        "",
        "Games end when a Command Center is destroyed, or both are destroyed simultaneously (draw).",
        "",
        "Build units, capture metal spots for faster spawning, and use tactical movement to outplay your opponent."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Selection & Movement",
      "lines": [
        "LEFT CLICK on a unit to select it. Hold SHIFT to add to selection.",
        "",
        "LEFT CLICK + DRAG draws a circle selection around multiple units.",
        "",
        "RIGHT CLICK + DRAG draws a movement path. Selected units are distributed along the path using nearest-neighbor assignment.",
        "",
        "RIGHT CLICK on a single point to move all selected units there.",
        "",
        "When a Command Center is selected, RIGHT CLICK sets a rally point for newly spawned units."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Combat & Fire Modes",
      "lines": [
        "Units with 'can_attack = True' automatically fire at enemies within range.",
        "",
        "Attacks are laser-based with damage, range, and cooldown stats.",
        "",
        "Command Centers also have a defensive laser that fires at nearby enemies.",
        "",
        "Medics do not attack but heal nearby friendly units instead.",
        "",
        "Combat is resolved every frame — position your units wisely to focus fire and avoid taking unnecessary damage."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Command Centers",
      "lines": [
        "Each team starts with one Command Center (CC).",
        "",
        "CCs spawn units every 10s. Click the GUI panel at the bottom to choose which unit type to spawn.",
        "",
        "CCs have a defensive laser (range 75, damage 20, cooldown 1s).",
        "",
